course: dictionary
lesson: 8004
title: Reduce: making things smaller
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Reduce means to make something smaller, less or weaker. Use the words around it to find the meaning. «Reduce by 5» in a maths sum means take away 5, so the number gets smaller.
explain: «Reducing waste helps most, because the waste is never made.» Here reduce means use less, so there is less rubbish. Check it by swapping in your meaning: "Making less waste helps most" still makes sense, so you have it right.
explain: The same word can mean different things in different places. In cooking, to reduce a sauce means boil it until it is thicker and smaller in amount. On a shop sign, a reduced price means it is cheaper. The setting tells you which meaning to use.
fact: Reduce means to make something smaller in size, amount, number or strength.
fact: «Reduce by half» means divide by 2, and «reduce by 5» means subtract 5.
fact: «Soft materials such as curtains and carpets absorb sound and reduce echoes.» Here reduce means make less.
fact: To reduce a fraction means to simplify it, so 6/8 becomes 3/4.
fact: «In reduced circumstances» is an old-fashioned UK phrase meaning poorer than before.
exercise: In maths, «reduce by 5» means what? | Multiply by 5 | Add 5 | *Subtract 5
exercise: «Reducing waste helps most, because the waste is never made.» What does reducing waste mean? | Recycling only plastic | *Using less, so there is less waste | Making more rubbish
exercise: A shop sign says «reduced price». What does it mean? | *It is cheaper | It is more expensive | It has been painted red
test: To reduce a fraction means what? | *To simplify it, so 6/8 becomes 3/4 | To make it bigger | To add it to another fraction
test: In cooking, what does «reduce a sauce» mean? | To pour it away | To cool it in the fridge | *To boil it until it is thicker and smaller in amount
exam: Which phrase means poorer than before? | reduce waste | *in reduced circumstances | reduced price | reduce speed
